    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been executed and recorded — **17 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary of failures\n\n**FT-19 — No persistence (most severe).** All admin work is held in memory only (localStorage empty). A created product and its subsequent edit vanished after reload: `/products` returned to \"9 products found\", the detail URL returned \"Product Not Found\", and admin showed only the 9 seeded products. This undermines the core \"curate your own lists\" premise.\n\n**CS-20 — Weak publish validation.** Only name, category, and short description are enforced. A product published successfully with no full review, no image, no retailer link, and zero specifications. A negative price (`-500`) also saved cleanly and rendered as \"-$500\"; only the rating bound (0–5) is enforced, via a native `min`/`max` attribute.\n\n**FT-4 — Tag filter list is hard-coded.** The Filters panel always shows the same 35 seeded tags. Newly assigned tags (`qa-added-tag`, `qazen`, …) never become filter choices, while removed tags (`wireless`, `premium`) remain listed and now return \"0 products found\". Notably, keyword search *does* pick up new tags — only the filter list is stale.\n\n**FT-2 — Featured set not fully browsable.** Marking/unmarking correctly updates the homepage section, but that section is capped at 3 cards and its \"View all\" link to `/products?featured=true` ignores the parameter, rendering all 10 products. With 4 featured items, the 4th was unreachable through any featured view.\n\n**IX-21 — Inert category selector on category pages.** On `/category/home`, choosing \"Fitness\" does nothing: URL, heading, product list, and the select itself all stay on Home Goods. The equivalent control on `/products` works correctly.\n\nNotable passing areas: search (case-insensitive across name, description, and tags), all four sort modes, price/rating/multi-tag filtering with correct OR semantics, detail page completeness, external purchase links, and not-found states.\n\nOne methodology note worth flagging: FT-1 passes strictly on \"saved changes are immediately reflected\" — I verified create and edit across all three categories within a single session. Its durability is what fails, and that is captured separately under FT-19, so the PASS should be read with that caveat."
